+# Coordinator cross-task domain-rank ruling for Task9/10 independent review
+
+2026-10-23. Root fullread original Task9 309lines SHA cf174e2a54827da3c2e2152dbddf7cfc292680882e676f0291fd1c014835c56b and Task10 276lines SHA fb0ea71f985ed280156ad88ea981c6f70ca5678e79043fef32c4f263e3b3e96f. Design candidates remain unadopted. This records a concrete cross-pair conflict/ruling, not a passing verdict or source qualification. Original files unchanged.
+
+Task9 section3.2 puts the minutes extension AFTER Task3/6 transcript-processing domain; Task10 section3 proposes saved-minutes domain before transcript-processing domain. Both cannot be the shared installed rank. Ruling: preserve established Task3/6 internal rank first; use Task9 concrete minutes extension afterward, before all original sessions/files/tasks/attempts/external operations. Common guard/info/roster/publication/final control roots after subject/meeting remain explicit shared control rank; do not lock external operation/execution rows with their publication headers.
+
+The minutes extension order is minutes_template -> template_revision -> exclusion_revision -> sensitive_exclusion -> generation_input -> minutes_revision -> element_set -> minutes_element -> action_item -> action_suggestion -> sensitive_detection -> background_note -> source_locator -> sensitive_detection_source -> background_note_source -> evidence_link -> result_review -> result_review_evidence -> final_result_review -> generation_candidate. Within each table fullPK ascending. Already-held exact rows are authenticated, never reacquired in another order. Final actual source-facade reconciliation must prove this complete shared rank executable, no alternative issuer/late existing-root acquisitions.
+
+PENDING headers may be discovered before locking, but their actual row locks occur at generation_candidate fixed rank, still BEFORE all sessions/files/tasks/attempts/external rows. A simple metadata writer need not lock unused transcript/minutes tables just to skip their ranks; a full graph operation must not lock candidate headers early and then lower-ranked actual domain rows later. B03 info/roster, Task4, Task6 and Task10/11 same shared contribution must declare dependencies before locking; overflow/changedset aborts rather than discovering late or installing a no-op. This ruling preserves Task10 requirement prelock before sources/tasks while resolving its earlier broad ordering proposal. Cost: finalsharedcoordinator must split declaration from actual ordered acquisition; independentreview must judge implementation feasibility, not waive it as facade detail.
+
+All producers/consumers use one qualified effective complete-domain budget for PENDING admission/prelock/disposition and relevant outstanding work; different proposed draft numbers are not independent permission limits. Actual effective minima and data dimensions are pinned/qualified before activation, no hidden truncation/productquota. Historical body/set remain independent; only currentroot/candidate/frozenfinal actualpair may be projected together. All nohash/archive/parse/I/O-under-root and private-holder/genuinegate constraints unchanged.
+
+Task9 routeprefix also requires source alignment: actual MeetingController and adopted Task6/10 prefix is /api/v1/meetings. Independentreview should judge Task9 /api/meetings routeproposal against actual authoritative path contract; this note does not silently rewrite that candidate or predetermine severity.
