++## 8. Definitive-zero-effect retry and explicit supersession extension
++
++### 8.1 Why a new confined operation is necessary
++
++Existing retryAfterZeroEffect checks old.spec businessVersion/cancelEpoch/input/fingerprint equality and operation logical key/hash equality. Changing destination changes logical fingerprint even with SAME final/business key; editing after safe failure changes r/final/key. Passing either to old retry is incompatible. Merely mutating publication current projection first would corrupt old task validation. This design adds a publication-only capability-confined method, leaves old retry behavior unchanged, and makes this an explicit independent review gate.
++
++Selected approach uses existing tables and immutable per-execution request_manifest to retain original logical facts. For same stable key, keep existing external_operation ID (unique kind/key prevents a second), advance its current request_hash/current_execution_no projection and append immutable execution. For a changed final/key, accept a new task for the SAME publication UUID; a NEW external_operation and first execution are created only by the later genuine committed marker. Preserve every old task/attempt/execution/final/request/receipt. Operation request_hash is documented as current-binding projection only on this new reviewed path, not historical truth. No update to historical execution manifests/hashes/proofs. Original operation fields/old behavior remain for all other task types.
++
++All old/new task policies in preparation must distinguish historical receipt-only closure from new current-effect eligibility; they must not demand that an old completed task match the new mutable publication projection merely to record its fact. This split stays private to publication and does not relax ordinary task validation. If pinned actual Task7 policy cannot verify old logical facts from a complete original manifest and attempt/final association, supersession MUST fail unavailable; root receives a concrete schema/protocol gap before implementation, never infers missing columns. New protocol manifests are mandatory from first Task11 publication; legacy/incomplete publication histories are not eligible for supersession or backfill.
++
++Prospective API on ExternalOperationPort, default fail-closed:
++
++```java
++PublicationReplacementAccepted replaceZeroEffectPublication(
++  PreparedPublicationReplacement prepared);
++```
++
++PreparedPublicationReplacement is a private issuer-bound carrier, constructed only by registered publication assembler after S/A. It binds publication ID/current publication revision, actor/current r/e/current final/request/render/destination assertion, exact original operation/execution/task/attempt history and outside-authenticated immutable proof-set digest, selected same-key/new-key mode and new full TaskSpec/manifest. DTO/boolean/FAILED/interface implementation alone cannot mint it. Engine authenticates issuer+same DataSource+actual holder+registered KNOWLEDGE_PUBLISH_V1 policy+purpose and entire prelocked old/new domain/spec union. No generic acquisition-mode fence relaxation or public callback.
++
++### 8.2 Local atomic sequence
++
++1. Replay-first explicit owner command lookup; MISS performs complete metadata S/A including every historical execution under publication, exact immutable receipt/proof verification and current final/destination readiness. No network under roots.
++2. One command TX (idempotency prelude, all identities/root/domain/source rows, ALL old/new tasks before any attempts, operations sorted then executions sorted) verifies expected meeting AND publication revision, current owner/r/e/final/readiness and exact full history/proof equality. Root prevents another retry/edit/submit. Check everpublished0, no mapping/no document success, no live/unknown/manual/quarantined/unsupported execution, every old execution terminal FAILED with complete verified zero-effect evidence and admitted locally applied failure. No future/unfinished task/attempt may escape inventory. Any late fact change aborts entire replacement.
++3. Same key: verify old operation current hash/spec against original immutable current execution manifest, then insert new task/full spec and PREPARED executionNo+1, update operation current request_hash to new logical digest, current_execution_no, state RETRY_QUEUED/reconcile_epoch+1/owner-expiry null. Its prior immutable request is still in each old execution manifest; never rewrite it. New key: insert only the new accepted task and update the publication current projection; all original operations remain terminal/history. V010 external_operation.marked_at is NOT NULL, so creating a pre-marker operation with a fictitious marked_at is forbidden. Later beginPrepared creates real operation/execution1 and actual marked_at atomically with its PUBLISH attempt. Same-key beginPrepared adopts the exact PREPARED execution above. All UUIDs/dependencies are declared before acquisition; actual FK order is respected.
++4. Update same publication current confirmation/key/library/folder/state READY/revision+1; old attempts retain prior confirmation/operation/execution. Do not advance content r or clear debt. Command receipt references actual new task ID and only associations already persisted (new-key executionId remains null until marker); audit/outbox flush last. All task/execution/operation/publication/receipt changes rollback together. No publication_attempt until real committed marker.
++5. Next marker rechecks complete cross-round state and current request, creates actual PUBLISH attempt then commits before send. The prepared bindingTransition carries expected prior provider slot generation+original receipt references; transport is one-shot under Task7. Marker ACK unknown no send; restart queries exact execution/publication slot, never issues replacement from memory.
