++### 8.3 Provider proof-CAS binding transition
++
++Stable-key slot may be rebound only by explicit `bindingTransition` containing previous publication slot generation, exact predecessor executions/request hashes/immutable zero-effect receipt IDs and new request identity. Provider authenticates its OWN durable stored proofs and checks publicationId-wide sole-document slot is empty, every prior accepted execution is irreversibly rejected with zero effect and no live/unknown work. Request assertion is not proof. Atomic provider transaction CASes generation, records new immutable binding/execution, and applies current ACL before document creation or definitive rejection. No separate pre-send side-effect scheduler/provisional binding request.
