++Same key/different body without explicit valid transition = conflict. Same execution repeat returns that execution's immutable original receipt; an old delayed POST after supersession never reopens it. Competing replacement requests with same expected slot: at most one binding wins; other conflict/UNKNOWN cannot create a document. Different final/business key still competes on SAME publicationId-wide document slot, ensuring one total document across history. Once document exists, all retries/replacements return existing verified document only when original binding matches, otherwise conflict; never another document or overwrite.
