+# Task 11 R1 — final confirmation, controlled publication and reconciliation design
+
+2026-10-23. **R1 full replacement for scoped independent rereview (T11DR-01/T11DR-02 only).** Original design and review are preserved unchanged. This revision adds explicit controlled caller/delegation/document-view authorization and genuine never-marked local failure/recovery with a minimal prospective accepted-binding model. No SQL/version is allocated or applied. **Prospective design for independent review.** This document selects executable contracts and future evidence gates. It does not adopt source, run tests, activate a provider or qualify Phase B. Only this R1 and its closure are written; no source/tests/DB/Docker/private environment/network/Git mutation/subagents.
+
+**Goal:** Complete saved minutes → exact human review → immutable final → durable controlled HTTP knowledge publication/reconciliation without duplicate remote effects or restored forbidden authority.
+
+**Architecture:** Reuse Tasks3/6/9/10 complete held facts and shared root; compute original-profile hashes outside roots, then consume a private one-use final writer in a fresh exact-recheck transaction. Publication consumes Task7 prepared marker/observation and single external owner, Task5 renewal drain, Task8 fair reconciliation, and a separately configured durable controlled KB provider. Remote facts and local application remain separate.
+
+**Implementation:** Future workers use executing-plans unless root expressly delegates. Root owns independent design/source review and activation; this document does not introduce a user-approval stall.
+
+## 1. Binding authority and actual source constraints
+
+Read first W/task-11-design-brief-prepared.md and task-11-plan-extract.md. W is `.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-23-ama-phase-b-remaining`. Binding: controlled-runtime NormativeR1, minutes contract/UX/config-wire and adopted authority-external-protocols/reconciliation-fairness/import-worker/saved-transcript/minutes-generation/minutes-editor wrappers under `docs/superpowers/specs/`, with exact upstream designs/reviews. Task7 root rulings and attempt-receipt clarification are mandatory. Task9 R1 and Task10 original are adopted designs, not source. Shared rank ruling SHA256 `3b10ab12f46f7b4a2f70a91871f20d4f4052662b1cfee2b08700b02188b6bc75` governs their merged domain order.
+
+Coordinator supplied adopted docs HEAD `875047cdbcd6ddd17f5c267f8998b7a5a4378b6c`. Task4 is changing the same tree; inspected working files are observations, not facade adoption. Root must pin actual adopted source/RAW hashes and reconcile concrete same-issuer/source/holder/gate APIs before source activation.
+
+Original product authority `designDocs/智能会议助手一期需求说明文档.md` lines869 and1030–1036 is binding: final-before-first-success permits returning to edit, changes invalidate final; zero-effect failed publication permits valid destination reconfiguration without another final if content unchanged, and changed content requires a new final; UNKNOWN first queries, never blindly retries. First verified success permanently prevents edits/republication even after withdrawal. This design preserves those requirements through an explicit proof-gated supersession branch (§8), not by permanently locking every FAILED state.
+
