+## 5. Shared authoritative freeze and reopening after zero effect
+
+Installed PublicationWriteGuard declares complete root/attempt/execution/mapping graph to every mutator. Missing helper, overflow, inconsistency/unknown states deny effects. Stage-only/everpublished=false/cached UI flag insufficient. Pure read/true acknowledgment is distinct. Special publication control capability private to Task7 policy, not browser MutationKind.
+
+| Actual durable facts | Shared mutation policy and allowed actions |
+|---|---|
+| No publication and never published | Ordinary owner CAS/lifecycle gates; final-before-publish may be edited, clearing final on version advance. |
+| READY/RUNNING/RECONCILING, PREPARED/RETRY_QUEUED/MARKED/UNKNOWN or any unresolved prior operation | Freeze content, intent, reference mutation, current/retained generation effects; status/query only, no resend/supersede. |
+| Terminal remote SUCCEEDED but raw attempt PENDING/UNKNOWN/unapplied | Freeze; remoteOutcome SUCCESS + applicationOutcome FENCED_MANUAL/manualLocked; no mapping/current success fabrication, no resend or claimable-reconciliation promise. |
+| FAILED and **every historical execution** verified terminal zero effect, locally admitted failure applied, no mapping/success/unknown/live work | Owner may edit normally (invalidates final), reconfigure destination with valid unchanged final, exact retry or proof-gated replacement (§8). Fresh complete proof under same root, not FAILED string alone. |
+| Fenced zero-effect failure with raw attempt unapplied, contradiction/MANUAL_REQUIRED/corrupt proof | Honest manual lock; no automatic application or retry. A separate fresh recorded-fact application protocol is outside this design. |
